 This install applies to "X-Wing" 1.0, an unofficial Amiga port of the 1993
 PC game by LucasArts and Totally Games.

 THIS IS AN EARLY ALPHA. The port runs the whole game, but it is not
 optimized yet: flight is slow even on fast processors, and a path the
 tests have not reached may stop with an error message. Bug reports are
 welcome (see Contact).


 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad version 17.0 or better and a PAL or NTSC
 Amiga with AGA and a 68020 or better; a 68030 or faster is recommended.
 The installed program uses 2 MB ChipMem and 8.5 MB OtherMem, including
 its Kickstart image, so it needs more than 8 MB Fast RAM: for example
 16 MB. The data cache needs the MMU: WHDLoad uses it on a 68040 or 68060,
 on a 68030 only with the WHDLoad option MMU (add the tooltype MMU to the
 icon).

 The game requires an installed A600/A1200/A4000 Kickstart 3.1 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick40063.A600", "kick40068.A1200" or "kick40068.A4000".
 Additionally the file "kick40063.A600.RTB", "kick40068.A1200.RTB" or
 "kick40068.A4000.RTB" must be installed in the same directory as the kickstart
 image. It can be found in the archive "util/boot/skick346.lha" on aminet.


 Installation:
 -------------
 The install does not include the original game files. It installs them from
 the five 1.44 MB PC floppies of X-Wing 1.0 (LucasArts, 1993). Other
 releases, such as the Collector's CD-ROM, are not supported. Run the Install
 icon and select a drawer containing either the disk images

   disk1.img  disk2.img  disk3.img  disk4.img  disk5.img

 or the files XWING.001 to XWING.005 copied from the disks, together with
 INSTALL.EXE, DETECT.EXE and READ.ME from disk 1. Every file is checked;
 damaged or other disks are refused. The game is installed as the original
 installer sets it up for AdLib sound.

 To update, select the same parent drawer and choose Keep. Use existing (the
 default) keeps the installed game files; Replace installs them again from the
 disks. Pilots and films are kept either way.


 Playing:
 --------
 Keyboard and mouse work as in the PC original; keys are at their US
 keyboard positions. See the original manual for the controls. There is no
 joystick support yet. Quit from the game's menus. The WHDLoad QuitKey
 (Help) quits immediately.


 History:
 --------
 version 0.1 (19.11.2026):
 - initial early alpha release: the whole game, with music and sound
   effects, unoptimized


